`resolveI18nLabel()` is duplicated here and in `packages/react/src/utils/i18n.ts`. To avoid drift (especially as the spec evolves), consider reusing a single shared implementation (e.g., export it from `@object-ui/react` or a shared utils package and import it into the console) instead of maintaining two copies.
```suggestion
import { resolveI18nLabel as baseResolveI18nLabel } from '../../packages/react/src/utils/i18n';

 * Resolves an I18nLabel to a plain string.
 * I18nLabel can be either a string or an object { key, defaultValue?, params? }.
 * When it's an object, we return the defaultValue or the key as fallback.
 * This delegates to the shared implementation in @object-ui/react to avoid drift.
 */
export function resolveI18nLabel(
  label: string | { key: string; defaultValue?: string; params?: Record<string, any> } | undefined,
): string | undefined {
  return baseResolveI18nLabel(label as any);
```
